---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="FAQ — N-Ops"
  description="Answers about N-Ops: pricing, self-hosting vs managed, agents, secrets, access control, audit and support."
  path="/faq"
>
<section class="sec" aria-labelledby="q-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="rgrid sh">
      <div class="sh-num" aria-hidden="true">?</div>
      <div class="sh-main">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="bar"></span>FAQ</p>
        <h1 id="q-h" class="text-[clamp(2.6rem,6vw,5.4rem)] leading-[.95] tracking-[-.05em]">Questions, <span class="grad-t">answered.</span></h1>
        <p class="sub">Everything people ask about running N-Ops: what it costs, how it works, and how your servers and secrets stay safe.</p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="rgrid mt-[clamp(36px,5vw,64px)]"><p class="eyebrow col-span-10 col-start-3 max-bp2:col-span-12 max-bp2:col-start-1 mb-5"><span class="bar"></span>The basics</p><div class="faq col-span-10 col-start-3 max-bp2:col-span-12 max-bp2:col-start-1 border-t-[1.5px] border-ink"><div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a1" id="q1"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">01</span>Is N-Ops free?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a1" role="region" aria-labelledby="q1"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Yes. N-Ops is open source under GNU GPL-V3.0, and self-hosting is free with every feature included. You only pay if you want us to run the control plane for you as a managed service.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a2" id="q2"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">02</span>What’s the difference between self-hosted and managed?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a2" role="region" aria-labelledby="q2"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">It's the same product. Self-hosted, you run the control plane on your own infrastructure and look after hosting, patching and upgrades yourself. With Managed Cloud we host, patch and upgrade it for you. Enterprise adds a dedicated, isolated instance, a 99.9% uptime SLA and a named engineer. In every case the agents run on your own servers.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a3" id="q3"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">03</span>How does Managed Cloud pricing work?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a3" role="region" aria-labelledby="q3"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Managed Cloud is usage-based and simple. The free tier is for a single user with your first 5 projects and 20 servers included. On a paid plan you get unlimited users and pay per extra project and per extra server beyond those included amounts. Admins can also cap the number of users, projects, services, variables and files, and servers for each organisation. Final prices and billing intervals are published with the managed service. Enterprise pricing is custom.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a4" id="q4"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">04</span>What stage is N-Ops at?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a4" role="region" aria-labelledby="q4"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">N-Ops is in active development. The Main API repository describes the full product direction, and not every capability there is finished or production-ready yet. Today the API covers sign-in and sessions, users and organisations, tags and permissions, and API keys, with a database schema for the secrets vault. Servers, agents, jobs and monitoring are on the roadmap. Check the releases and issues on GitHub for what is available in each build.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a5" id="q5"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">05</span>Who maintains N-Ops?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a5" role="region" aria-labelledby="q5"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">N-Ops is built by Neko Nik in partnership with YSPL (Yukthi Systems Private Limited), together with the open-source community on GitHub.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a6" id="q6"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">06</span>What is N-Ops built with?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a6" role="region" aria-labelledby="q6"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">The Main API is written in Rust on Actix Web, stores its data in PostgreSQL, uses an in-memory or Redis cache, and RabbitMQ for messaging. Secrets are encrypted with AES-GCM and passwords are hashed with bcrypt. The whole thing is licensed under GNU GPL-V3.0.</p></div></div>
</div></div></div><div class="rgrid mt-[clamp(36px,5vw,64px)]"><p class="eyebrow col-span-10 col-start-3 max-bp2:col-span-12 max-bp2:col-start-1 mb-5"><span class="bar"></span>Running it</p><div class="faq col-span-10 col-start-3 max-bp2:col-span-12 max-bp2:col-start-1 border-t-[1.5px] border-ink"><div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a7" id="q7"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">07</span>How do I run N-Ops myself?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a7" role="region" aria-labelledby="q7"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">The Main API is published as a Docker image at neko7nik/n-ops-main-api on Docker Hub, pulled with docker pull neko7nik/n-ops-main-api:TAG. For production, pin a specific tag instead of latest, keep data on persistent volumes, restrict API and agent network access, keep secrets out of source control and image layers, and back up your data and test the restore. Source-install instructions will be published once the startup process is settled, so avoid guessed commands.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a8" id="q8"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">08</span>Is it ready for production?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a8" role="region" aria-labelledby="q8"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Treat it carefully. Until a security review and production-readiness statement are published, evaluate the current implementation yourself before trusting it with production credentials or infrastructure. Never paste real secrets, private keys or credentials into GitHub issues or public discussions.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a9" id="q9"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">09</span>How can I contribute or report a problem?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a9" role="region" aria-labelledby="q9"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Bug reports, feature proposals, documentation fixes and integrations are welcome on the Main API repository. Check existing issues first, then describe the problem, how to reproduce it, the version or commit you are on, and relevant logs with secrets removed.</p></div></div>
</div></div></div><div class="rgrid mt-[clamp(36px,5vw,64px)]"><p class="eyebrow col-span-10 col-start-3 max-bp2:col-span-12 max-bp2:col-start-1 mb-5"><span class="bar"></span>Servers and agents</p><div class="faq col-span-10 col-start-3 max-bp2:col-span-12 max-bp2:col-start-1 border-t-[1.5px] border-ink"><div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a10" id="q10"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">10</span>What is an agent?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a10" role="region" aria-labelledby="q10"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">A small program you install on each Linux server. It connects that server to your control plane, reports its OS, kernel, CPU architecture and hostname, and runs the jobs your team approves. N-Ops tracks each agent's connectivity and last-seen time, and if the connection drops the agent reconnects and recovers on its own.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a11" id="q11"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">11</span>What can N-Ops manage?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a11" role="region" aria-labelledby="q11"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Linux servers through the agent, containers through Docker or Podman (list, start, stop, restart, pull, and inspect images, networks and volumes), Compose projects and their files, system services, remote files and terminals. Jobs can be commands, scripts or Ansible playbooks, and you group servers with names, labels and tags such as test, staging and production.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a12" id="q12"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">12</span>What does monitoring cover?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a12" role="region" aria-labelledby="q12"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Built-in host metrics include CPU, load average, memory, swap, disk capacity and I/O, network traffic, uptime and agent health. Extensions can add custom metrics and checks, for example a Postfix extension that alerts when the mail queue grows too long. Metrics are planned to be stored as Parquet files, rotated at a set row count. Offline-server detection and email alerts come first.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a13" id="q13"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">13</span>What happens when a server goes offline?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a13" role="region" aria-labelledby="q13"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">The control plane notices and emails you, and that server's jobs stay in its queue. When the agent reconnects it picks up the next job in order, so nothing runs out of sequence. Agents also reconnect and recover on their own, and are designed to update through a controlled, automatic mechanism.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a14" id="q14"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">14</span>Can I use a terminal and manage files from the browser?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a14" role="region" aria-labelledby="q14"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Yes, that is the plan. A browser terminal gives you a real shell on a server, and the file manager lets you browse, create, edit and delete files, transfer them between your machine and a server, move them from one server to another, and copy in config files from the secrets vault. Admins can require approval for file read, create, edit and delete, and allow or block uploads and downloads separately.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a15" id="q15"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">15</span>How do I control what each server allows?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a15" role="region" aria-labelledby="q15"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Every server has its own settings: a server type and a unique Join ID, whether remote commands, file transfer, monitoring and container management are allowed, which container actions (start, stop, restart, remove) are permitted, and a list of sensitive commands that need admin approval first. You can also limit users to named Linux accounts.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a16" id="q16"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">16</span>How do jobs and rollouts work?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a16" role="region" aria-labelledby="q16"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Each server has its own first-in, first-out queue with priorities, manual reordering and concurrency limits. Jobs are acknowledged, tracked and show live output, and failed jobs retry with exponential backoff and jitter. Duplicate-execution protection, timeouts, cancel, pause and resume are part of the design. Canary and staged rollouts let you try a few servers first, with rollback.</p></div></div>
</div></div></div><div class="rgrid mt-[clamp(36px,5vw,64px)]"><p class="eyebrow col-span-10 col-start-3 max-bp2:col-span-12 max-bp2:col-start-1 mb-5"><span class="bar"></span>Secrets and access</p><div class="faq col-span-10 col-start-3 max-bp2:col-span-12 max-bp2:col-start-1 border-t-[1.5px] border-ink"><div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a17" id="q17"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">17</span>How are secrets organised?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a17" role="region" aria-labelledby="q17"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Resources follow one path: Organisation, Project, Environment, Service, then variables and files. Development, staging and production stay separate, and you can use plain environment variables or write-only secrets that can never be revealed. Secrets keep a version history with rollback, bulk editing, .env import and export, and Docker Compose secrets support.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a18" id="q18"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">18</span>How are secrets protected?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a18" role="region" aria-labelledby="q18"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Secrets are encrypted with AES-256-GCM, an authenticated encryption mode. Every change creates a new version, only people with the reveal permission can see values, and every access is written to the audit log. Apps and agents fetch secrets with read-only API keys scoped to a project, environment, service or chosen variables. Secrets are never written to logs in plaintext.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a19" id="q19"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">19</span>How is access controlled?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a19" role="region" aria-labelledby="q19"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Role-based access control works per organisation and resource, with fine-grained permissions such as tag:view, tag:create, tag:edit and tag:delete. Sign-in is designed for multi-factor options: email, TOTP, physical security keys, FIDO2 and WebAuthn. You can restrict where sign-ins come from, allow only named users to run commands, and require an admin to approve sensitive operations first.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a20" id="q20"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">20</span>What does the audit log record?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a20" role="region" aria-labelledby="q20"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Who started an operation, what it targeted and what happened, including sign-ins, approvals, jobs, remote commands and secret reveals. Logs are kept for 90 days and can be filtered by date, user or action type. Sensitive values are redacted, authorised users can download them from the web app, and a workflow can export them on a schedule. Scheduled exports can be emailed to the people you choose.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a21" id="q21"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">21</span>What else is planned?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a21" role="region" aria-labelledby="q21"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">PostgreSQL management with simple queries, and more services such as RabbitMQ and Redis later; custom, user-defined service logs; linking a GitHub account for repository and Actions integration; backup workflows; and client libraries for Rust, Python, Go and JavaScript. These are product direction, not release commitments.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a22" id="q22"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">22</span>Are there secure notes?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a22" role="region" aria-labelledby="q22"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Yes, planned. The first release covers creating and managing simple notes. You can share a note read-only inside your organisation, or share it by link with an optional expiry and password. A note protected by a password is encrypted with it; a note saved without one is stored as plain text, so use that only for things that are not sensitive.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a23" id="q23"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">23</span>What can admins manage?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a23" role="region" aria-labelledby="q23"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">The Admin area covers the organisation, users, API keys, roles, tags and the audit logs. API keys reuse the same roles, so there is no separate permission model to learn. Tags group resources and drive who can see what.</p></div></div>
</div></div></div><div class="rgrid mt-[clamp(36px,5vw,64px)]"><p class="eyebrow col-span-10 col-start-3 max-bp2:col-span-12 max-bp2:col-start-1 mb-5"><span class="bar"></span>Approvals and automation</p><div class="faq col-span-10 col-start-3 max-bp2:col-span-12 max-bp2:col-start-1 border-t-[1.5px] border-ink"><div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a24" id="q24"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">24</span>How do approvals work?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a24" role="region" aria-labelledby="q24"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Anyone can raise an approval under a tag, for one or several servers. It is pending until an admin approves or rejects it, has an expiry, and carries a chat thread where people can discuss it, mention each other and attach files or references. When the status changes, the right people are notified, the thread and the audit log are updated, and any dependent workflow can continue. Once an approval is approved or rejected it cannot be changed or deleted, and expired approvals are removed automatically, at the latest 90 days after they were created.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a25" id="q25"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">25</span>What are workflows?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a25" role="region" aria-labelledby="q25"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">A visual, flow-based automation builder. You connect building blocks into a flow that can use the vault, metrics and remote execution. For example: every 10 seconds check server health and alert if it is unhealthy, or every minute read the mail queue, turn the output into a number and alert if it passes a threshold.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a26" id="q26"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">26</span>Which building blocks do workflows have?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a26" role="region" aria-labelledby="q26"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Alert (email, API call or in-app notification), If condition (boolean, comparison, logical, string, numeric, date and presence checks), Remote execution on one or many servers (one by one, in parallel or as a canary), Ansible playbooks, API calls, a Parser that turns text into JSON or numbers, and AI steps. Execution and API steps can wait for admin approval and use secrets from the vault; AI steps cannot see secrets.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a27" id="q27"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">27</span>Can I send my own metrics?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a27" role="region" aria-labelledby="q27"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Yes. You can post a JSON payload with custom metrics to the monitoring endpoint, then view, filter, graph and export them next to the built-in infrastructure metrics.</p></div></div>
</div></div></div><div class="rgrid mt-[clamp(36px,5vw,64px)]"><p class="eyebrow col-span-10 col-start-3 max-bp2:col-span-12 max-bp2:col-start-1 mb-5"><span class="bar"></span>Getting help</p><div class="faq col-span-10 col-start-3 max-bp2:col-span-12 max-bp2:col-start-1 border-t-[1.5px] border-ink"><div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a28" id="q28"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">28</span>How does a request move through N-Ops?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a28" role="region" aria-labelledby="q28"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Someone on your team asks for something in the web app or API. The control plane checks who they are and whether their role allows it, queues the work for the right server, and the agent there runs it. The result comes back to your screen and every step is recorded in the audit log. The Architecture section on the home page walks through each step.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="qa group border-b border-line">
<h3 class="[font-size:inherit] [letter-spacing:inherit] [line-height:inherit] [font-weight:inherit]"><button class="group/btn w-full grid grid-cols-[3.2rem_1fr_40px] max-bp3:grid-cols-[1.8rem_1fr_36px] items-center gap-[var(--gut)] py-[26px] max-bp3:py-5 font-semibold tracking-[-.03em] leading-[1.15] text-[clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.75rem)]" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="a29" id="q29"><span class="n font-mono text-xs leading-none text-mute">29</span>Where do I get help?<span class="pm w-10 h-10 max-bp3:w-9 max-bp3:h-9 rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-line-2 relative transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/btn:border-ink group-aria-expanded/btn:bg-mint group-aria-expanded/btn:border-mint before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-1/2 before:top-1/2 before:w-3.5 before:h-0.5 before:bg-ink before:-translate-x-1/2 before:-translate-y-1/2 group-aria-expanded/btn:before:bg-ink-f after:content-[''] after:absolute after:left-1/2 after:top-1/2 after:w-3.5 after:h-0.5 after:bg-ink after:-translate-x-1/2 after:-translate-y-1/2 after:rotate-90 after:transition-transform after:duration-[400ms] after:ease-std group-aria-expanded/btn:after:bg-ink-f group-aria-expanded/btn:after:rotate-0" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="ans grid grid-rows-[0fr] transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-500 ease-std group-[.open]:grid-rows-[1fr]" id="a29" role="region" aria-labelledby="q29"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="pb-7 pl-[calc(3.2rem+var(--gut))] max-bp3:pl-0 text-ink-2 text-[17px] max-w-[760px]">Self-hosted users get community support on GitHub. Managed Cloud includes email support. Enterprise adds priority support, a named engineer and guided onboarding.</p></div></div>
</div></div></div>
